        "agm_result": "Agenda #1: Shareholders approved the 2025 Annual Report, Financial Statements, and Board of Commissioners' Oversight Report, while granting a full discharge of liability to the Directors and Commissioners.\nAgenda #2: The meeting resolved not to distribute cash dividends and instead allocated the entire 2025 net profit to be recorded as retained earnings.\nAgenda #3: The meeting approved 2026 salaries for Commissioners to remain the same or increase by a maximum of 15% and authorized the Board of Commissioners to determine Director compensation.\nAgenda #4: Authority was granted to the Board of Commissioners to appoint a Registered Public Accounting Firm to audit the 2026 financial statements and establish the terms and honorarium.\nAgenda #5: Corporate Secretary Alexsandro Martin Tiga submitted an official electronic cover note for the 2026 Annual General Meeting of Shareholders on April 28, 2026, though specific decisions are not stated."
